WEBVTT

00:00:02.447 --> 00:00:07.167
And I started from like the ground up where I knew nothing and

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:10.747
I was building something to where I feel like...

00:00:10.447 --> 00:00:11.767
Like you literally built the machine.

00:00:11.974 --> 00:00:14.994
And so I had to understand.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:19.194
I think like people coming into the lab in a semester when things

00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:21.167
have been built, and they're just kind of like,

00:00:21.207 --> 00:00:23.400
I never got the chance to learn any of this.

00:00:23.687 --> 00:00:29.487
And then the feedback cycle can become, that didn't work, try

00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:29.827
again.

00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:30.167
Yeah.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:31.500
That didn't work, try again.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:37.980
AI could write the first draft of a paper that then we read

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.333
and really understand

00:00:39.586 --> 00:00:43.566
Xavier was explaining the Bayesian optimization to Seth and

00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:46.626
I was listening in and I could tell that Xavier really understood

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:50.067
that he wasn't just using AI to do the learning
